  "notes": "USAGE:\nUsed as a suru verb ({看護|かんご}する = to nurse, to care for) or as a noun modifier ({看護|かんご}{師|し} = nurse). The most common compound is {看護師|かんごし} (nurse), which replaced the older gender-specific terms {看護婦|かんごふ} (female nurse) and {看護士|かんごし} (male nurse) in 2002.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {看護師|かんごし}: nurse\n- {看護|かんご}{学校|がっこう}: nursing school\n- {看護|かんご}{学部|がくぶ}: nursing faculty/department\n- {看護|かんご}{記録|きろく}: nursing records\n- {在宅|ざいたく}{看護|かんご}: home nursing care\n- {看護|かんご}にあたる: to provide nursing care\n\nWATCH OUT:\n- {漢語|かんご}: Chinese-origin word (linguistic term, different meaning)",
